GJEB for Horizon
================

This Horizon mod is a port of idea, not of code: it reimplements the behaviour of

  GJEB (GammaJustExtremeBright) — https://modrinth.com/mod/gjeb
  Copyright (c) the GJEB contributors, Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/MC-U-Team/GJEB-GammaJustExtremeBright

whose brightness slider reaches 1000% instead of vanilla's 100%, so a player can see in the dark
without torches or night vision. No line of the Java mod was copied: Horizon runs Rust, and this
mod is written against the Horizon mod API 0.2 and the native mixin route.

Prior art on Horizon, read for its approach (also MIT, not copied):

  MoreGamma / fullbright — https://github.com/bezi5kt/gamma-rust
  Copyright (c) 2026 tilen, MIT License

The approach both share: the game copies the brightness slider into the renderer's lightmap gamma;
this mod overwrites that value once per frame while it is on, and leaves the player's own brightness
slider and options.txt untouched, so switching it off restores the player's brightness immediately.

The icon is original artwork drawn for this mod.
